      "releaseNotes": "• Practise keeping the beat while you hear the click between beats with Displaced click.\n• Choose from eight click sounds, including five new ones. Adjust their pitch and hear percussion accents more clearly.\n• If you hear this device's click after the others in Share click, you can adjust the offset to line them up..\n• Clearer help when you can't join Share click, plus fixes to Tempo trainer and full screen.",
      "version": "1.1",
      "wrapperType": "software",
      "currency": "EUR",
      "description": "GigClick is a metronome for musicians, built by a drummer. It gives solo players and full bands a dependable pulse, with meters counted the way musicians use them and setlists you can run on stage.\n\nROCK SOLID FROM THE FIRST BAR TO THE LAST\n20 to 300 BPM, set with the slider, tap tempo or ±1 and ±5 controls. The click keeps playing with the screen locked or the app in the background, and changes apply while it runs. Audio latency on Bluetooth devices is automatically adjusted for, with manual adjustment as a backup.  GigClick remembers the offset for each device.\n\nMETERS COUNTED THE WAY MUSICIANS USE THEM\nPresets for 2/4, 3/4, 4/4, 5/4, 6/8 and 7/8, with 6/8 counted in two and 7/8 grouped 2+2+2+1. Build custom meters up to 16 with your own grouping, such as 2+2+3 or 3+3+3+2. The BPM always shows which note it counts, so the BPM gives the tempo you expect.\n\nSEE THE COUNT\nA large beat count shows every click, 1 e & a, with the accent flashing in your chosen colour. Full screen mode keeps the count, the current song and the setlist controls in view.\n\nSONGS AND SETLISTS YOU CAN RUN ON STAGE\n• Save the tempo, meter, click pattern, accents and notes for each song, in folders\n• Give a song a structure: sections that each have their own bars, tempo and meter, changing on the bar\n• Build setlists, drag to reorder, and step through them with large previous and next controls\n• See the song notes, your position and the next song while you play\n• Queue songs on the fly, then save the queue as a setlist\n• Export any setlist as a printable PDF\n• Back up and restore your library\n\nSHARE ONE CLICK ACROSS THE BAND\nConnect the band's phones to the leader's phone to share their click. Join on the same Wi-Fi network or hotspot by scanning its QR code or entering its address and joining code. Each device plays its own click sound and volume while the leader controls the tempo, meter and start/stop, and followers see the current song, notes, setlist position and next song. No account or internet server is involved. Session traffic is not encrypted, so avoid sensitive song or setlist notes.\n\nPRACTICE\n• Subdivisions: quarter notes, eighths, triplets or sixteenths\n• Per-beat accents: make any beat loud, normal or silent, for example a click on 2 and 4 only\n• Gap training: choose how many bars play and how many are silent, then check where you land\n• Tempo trainer: set the tempo to increase automatically while you play, say +2 BPM every 8 bars, to build speed\n• Displaced click: practise keeping the beat while you hear the click between beats. Choose sixteenths or triplets in 2/4, 3/4, 4/4 or 5/4\n• Practice guides: short exercises on subdivisions, Gap training, Displaced click and Tempo trainer, each able to set up the metronome for you\n\nMAKE IT YOURS\nEight click sounds (Classic, Woodblock, Soft, Cowbell, Rimshot, Clave, Hi-hat and Shaker), adjustable click pitch and volume, six accent colours and beat-flash strength. Audio, visual or combined output. A dark interface made for dark stages.\n\nPay once. No ads. No account.\nNo subscriptions and no tracking. GigClick collects no data, and your library stays on your device.",
